# Optional headless configuration for Vault.
#
# Copy to .env in this app's app-data directory on the Umbrel server:
#   ~/umbrel/app-data/zambon-vault/.env
# or into the Vault folder itself:
#   ~/umbrel/home/Apps/Vault/.env
# (the Vault folder is also the app's config dir, so this file sits next to
# colecionary.json and survives app uninstall/reinstall)
#
# Leave both values unset to let the first-run setup wizard configure the app.
# Setting them skips the wizard.

# SQL Server 2022 or newer. Use the Umbrel server's LAN IP as the host: this
# app is not on the sql-server network, so "sql-server-2025" will not resolve.
#ConnectionStrings__Vault=Server=192.168.1.10,1433;Database=Colecionary;User Id=sa;Password=SqlServer2025!;TrustServerCertificate=true

# Must be at least 32 characters.
#Jwt__SigningKey=

# ImageStorage__Root is not settable here: docker-compose.yml pins it to the
# Vault folder so uploaded images survive app updates, and values in
# docker-compose.yml override this file.

# --- Optional, added in 1.6.0 -------------------------------------------

# The sign-in throttle counts failures per account and per calling address.
# This app publishes port 7001 directly, so a LAN client's own address is what
# arrives and the address rule works as intended. Put a reverse proxy or a
# tunnel (the Cloudflared app, for instance) in front of it and every caller
# arrives as the proxy: thirty failed logins from anyone would then answer 429
# to everybody. Name the proxy's container IP to have Vault read
# X-Forwarded-For instead. Leave unset with no proxy in front -- trusting the
# header unconditionally lets a caller name its own address, which is worse
# than having no address rule at all.
#ForwardedHeaders__KnownProxies__0=172.18.0.5

# Photos nothing points at any more are marked with the date they stopped being
# referenced; the collector deletes them once that mark has stood for the whole
# grace period. It is the only thing in the app that destroys data
# irreversibly, so it is off by default and, once enabled, still only writes a
# report to the log until DryRun is turned off too.
#ImageGc__Enabled=true
#ImageGc__DryRun=false
#ImageGc__GracePeriod=30.00:00:00
